Part 1 — Interview Concept
    Suppose I give you:
                        intervals = [
                            [1,3],
                            [2,6],
                            [8,10],
                            [9,12]
                        ]


        And ask:        
                  Merge all overlapping intervals.
        
        Expected result:
                    [1,6]
                    [8,12]
First question :     Would you immediately start comparing every interval with every other interval?

                      No.

First ask:     Can sorting make the problem easier?

                Yes.

Sort intervals by their starting point:

=====================================================================================================================================================================
                                    [1,3]
                                    [2,6]
                                    [8,10]
                                    [9,12]
They are already sorted here.
Now observe:
              [1,3]
              [2,6]
They overlap because:   2 <= 3
So merge:   [1,6]

Then:
      [8,10]
      [9,12]
Again:   9 <= 10

Merge:   [8,12]





